WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
A plane is coming in to land.

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.950
Through the cockpit window, the
ground rushes up to meet it.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.290
In seconds, she must judge her height,
her speed and where the wheels will touch.

4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.350
Her main clue: the ground
streaming past the window.

5
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.840
So how can a rushing, moving
view be enough to land a plane?

6
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.360
In this mission, you'll meet
Gibson's theory of how we see,

7
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.800
and find out what he thought
our eyes really have to go on.

8
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.380
You'll see how moving changes
the view in a regular way.

9
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:35.270
From a train, the fence flashes past
while distant hills barely move.

10
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: explain how a moving
view can be enough to land a plane.
